  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116424",
      "title": "Loading Data Based On Route Parameters In Child Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 280,
      "videoOrder": 267,
      "sourceHash": "befa610ed21c17340fb5a2810d54e47182abcea1591e9fcf5e478a21d5db0349",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "So how can we load the tasks for a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 5.91,
          "en": "with help of that user ID?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.91,
          "end": 10.21,
          "en": "Well, as a first step, I'll inject the tasks service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "by calling, inject",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 16.803,
          "en": "and injecting the TaskService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.3,
          "end": 23.3,
          "en": "And with that done, user tasks here can actually be set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "to a computed Signal here, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "since I'm using Signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "Otherwise you could use a gather, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 33.54,
          "en": "But here I'm using computed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.54,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "And then in there we want to reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 40.91,
          "en": "to the TasksService, access the allTasks Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 45.18,
          "en": "and then we can call filter on that array of tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.18,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "that's managed by this Signal to find all the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 51.093,
          "en": "that belong to this user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "So, filter will execute a function on every task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "in this allTasks array in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "And I wanna filter out and get all the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 68.237,
          "en": "where the userId is equal to this.userId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 74.46000000000001,
          "en": "And since I'm reading the allTasks Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 74.46000000000001,
          "end": 79.02,
          "en": "and the userId Signal in this computed Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 79.02,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "Angular will automatically recompute this Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 86.283,
          "en": "whenever the tasks or the user ID changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 90.75,
          "en": "And, as mentioned before, alternatively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "if you're not using Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 94.5,
          "en": "or if you don't want to use this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.5,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "you could, of course, also set up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 101.31,
          "en": "to the parent map, as you saw it before, and use observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.31,
          "end": 105.93,
          "en": "and regular properties for getting your user tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 109.593,
          "en": "Here I'll use the input and this computed Signal, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 110.72999999999999,
          "end": 113.55,
          "en": "And with that, we just need to read the userTasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 115.11,
          "en": "here in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.11,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "And if you then save it all, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 122.763,
          "en": "that for different users, different tasks are being loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.99,
          "end": 126.69,
          "en": "And that's, therefore now, the behavior I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 126.69,
          "end": 129.27,
          "en": "As a next step we can therefore make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 129.27,
          "end": 133.023,
          "en": "that we also allow users to add new tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
